      "message": "fix(app): a gone plate lets go of its riders; refuse a 45-degree turned plate\n\nReview of PR #823:\n- DeleteFixture, DeleteEntity, UntagFixture and a grid-dropping\n  ImportFixture clear the direct riders' plate mounts in the same command\n  (snapshotted; undo restores plate and mounts). A later plate given the\n  freed name no longer carries fixtures never placed on it. Load drops\n  (and logs) a place naming a plate the file does not hold.\n- Detection refuses a staggered read on a plate whose edges don't run\n  along X/Y (a square grid turned exactly 45 degrees); fit refusals name\n  the likely cause (holes not lined up with X/Y: turned or irregular).\n- Grid law: nearest holes more than a diameter apart, pitch above twice\n  the 0.05 mm snap tolerance.\n- MoveFixture on a plate clash-checks the riders it carries.\n\nPinned by fixture_plate_riders (5 tests) and\nfixture_plate_detect::a_turned_plate_is_refused_naming_the_turn.\n\nRefs #819\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
